# `golem/inspector`

**Agent (`golem/inspector`):** `Attach(ctx, srv, schema, opts)` dials the hub's `/ws/agent` with a bearer token, registers the generated `InspectorSchema()`, and stays idle until the hub sends `ObserveStart`. It reads entities only inside `Server.ObserveReplication` callbacks on the tick goroutine: a snapshot from `All()`/`FullUpdate()`, then per-entity dirty masks accumulated from `LastFlushMask()` and encoded with `MarshalDeltaMask` at most `RateHz` per second. Every full state carries the entity's space (`EntityState.space`, from `EntitySpace`, omitted for 0); `ReplicationFrame.Moved` entries coalesce per window into `Batch.moves` (latest space), dropped for entities removed in the window or sent as full states; a move whose entity also has a delta is appended right after that delta in the same batch (batch splits never separate them), and only moves without a delta follow the removals. Snapshots and batches are queued as single items; a full queue drops the stream and restarts it with a new epoch. It never blocks the tick loop, never filters by interest, visibility or ownership, and is disabled when `HubURL` is empty. `OptionsFromEnv` logs malformed Inspector settings by name without exposing their values, keeps valid label pairs, and leaves the rate at its default for invalid `GOLEM_INSPECTOR_RATE_HZ` values.

**Wire (`golem/inspector/wire`):** hand-written codec for `inspector.proto` on top of `golem/pb.Writer` with a bounds-checked reader (decoders return errors, never panic). Owns the `Schema` descriptor and `EntityFields`, the game-agnostic merge of generated State/Delta messages (a set mask bit whose field is absent resets it). `testdata/` golden fixtures are shared with the TypeScript codec in `golem-inspector/`; regenerate with `go test ./golem/inspector/wire -update` and rerun `npm test` there after any protocol change. `ProtocolVersion` stays 1 for additive fields (receivers skip unknown fields, but the envelope version must match exactly); keep zero values unencoded so older traffic stays byte-identical.

**Hub (`golem/inspector/hub`):** target registry, per-target world store (merged fields plus each entity's space; moves for unknown entities are dropped), cold-observation refcount with grace stop, per-browser bounded queues with resync/slow-consumer handling, shared-password sessions, JSON REST, metrics and static UI hosting. All state is under one mutex; sockets are written only by their own writer goroutines.

**Boundaries:** `wire` and `hub` must not import `golem` (the hub binary stays free of the runtime). Only the agent imports `golem`. Runtime hooks the agent needs belong in `golem/replication_observer.go`, not in agent-specific code inside the tick loop. The inspector is read-only and entity-only.
